ous gastrointestinal issues, including diarrhea and inflammatory bowel disease. By fostering a healthy gut microbiome, prebiotics contribute to overall digestive health and may offer therapeutic benefits for individuals suffering from these conditions.", "LEVOFLOXACINO:Levofloxacino is another quinolone antibiotic that can be used to treat severe cases of diarrhea caused by bacterial infections.", "AZITROMICINA:Azitromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that may be used in cases of acute diarrhea when bacterial infection is suspected.", "ERITROMICINA:Eritromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that is utilized to treat various bacterial infections, including those that may lead to acute diarrhea. It is particularly effective in critical care patients and can assist in facilitating the passage of a feeding tube through the digestive system. However, it is important to note that eritromicina should be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. Additionally, the antibiotic can be associated with the production of diarrhea as a side effect. It is also noteworthy that eritromicina can be degraded in an acidic environment, which may impact its absorption.", "FECAL MICROBIOTA TRANSPLANTATION:Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) is a procedure being researched for the treatment of severe and recurrent diarrhea caused by Clostridium difficile.", "QUINOLONES:", "PAÍSES EN VÍAS DE DESARROLLO:Developing countries where infectious causes are more prevalent in cases of chronic diarrhea.", "F75:F75 is a special nutritional treatment formula used for severe acute malnutrition associated with diarrhea in children, administered orally or via a nasogastric tube.", "F100:F100 is another special nutritional treatment formula for severe acute malnutrition, similar to F75, used in pediatric cases.", "PLÁTANOS:Bananas are recommended for patients with diarrhea due to their potassium content and ability to help firm stools.", "VEGETALES COCIDOS:Cooked vegetables are advised for patients with diarrhea as they provide essential nutrients while being easier to digest.", "INTOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA:Lactose intolerance can develop secondary to infectious enteritis, affecting dietary choices during recovery from diarrhea.", "ALMIDÓN COCIDO:", "COLITIS ULCEROSA:Colitis ulcerosa, also known as ulcerative colitis (UC), is an autoimmune disease and a form of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) that primarily affects the colon and rectum. It is characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucosa and submucosa, leading to a range of symptoms including rectal bleeding, abdominal pain, and chronic diarrhea. The condition can result in significant gastrointestinal distress and may lead to nutritional deficits and problems with nutrient absorption, particularly during acute flare-ups. Colitis ulcerosa is a chronic condition that requires ongoing management and may necessitate nutritional intervention to address complications arising from the disease.", "VASCULITIS:La vasculitis es una inflamación de los vasos sanguíneos que puede afectar el sistema digestivo y contribuir a la diarrea crónica.", "ANÁLISIS DE HECES:El análisis de heces es una prueba diagnóstica que puede ayudar a identificar la causa de la diarrea crónica."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}